♻️ **DEBT**: The missing-parameter branch is unreachable — `ParamMap.get()` returns `null`, never `undefined`.

<details>
<summary>Details and fix</summary>

A genuinely absent `organizationId` yields `null`, falls past this check into `isId<OrganizationId>(null)` (which returns `false`, since `isId` starts with `typeof id === "string"`), and throws `"Invalid OrganizationId provided in route parameter"` — the wrong diagnostic for a missing param.

```suggestion
    const orgIdParam = this.route.snapshot.paramMap.get("organizationId");
    if (orgIdParam == null) {
      throw new Error("`organizationId` is a required route parameter");
    }
```

Loose `== null` covers both. Not user-visible today since no route renders this component yet, but it will be once the org route lands per the PM-41469 TODO above.
</details>

